          "path": "_m/u/1/5/1/expo-58-wp/stamp-belgium-1958-com.jpg",
          "filename": "BEL 1958 MiNr1091 pm B002.jpg",
          "caption": "Stamp of Belgium; 1958; commemorative stamp of the issue \"World Exhibition 1958 in Brussels\"; stamp motive show a view to the Atomium in Brussels and the exhibition emblem; stamp postmarked in Brussels, 1958\nNote:\nThe \"Atomium\" is a momument in Laeken near Brussels, erected to the there \"World Exhibition 1958\". The designer of this monument was the engeneer André Waterkeyn (1917-2005). The construction symbolizes a body-centered cubic crystal structure. Erected was the monument by the architects André and Jean Polak in 1957 at the Heysel-Plateau in Laeken near Brussels.\nStamp: Michel: No. 1091 ; Yvert &amp; Tellier: No. 1008A; Scott: No. 501; AFA: 1108\nColor: dark green\nWatermark: none\nNominal value: 2 F 50 (= 2.50 Francs)\nPostage validity: from 4 February 1958 until ?\n\nStamp picture size (printed area of a single stamp): 24.5 x 35.5 mm",
          "alt": "Stamp of Belgium; 1958; commemorative stamp of the issue \"World Exhibition 1958 in Brussels\"; stamp motive show a view to the Atomium in Brussels and the exhibition emblem; stamp postmarked in Brussels, 1958\nNote:\nThe \"Atomium\" is a momument in Laeken near Brussels, erected to the there \"World Exhibition 1958\". The designer of this monument was the engeneer André Waterkeyn (1917-2005). The construction symbolizes a body-centered cubic crystal structure. Erected was the monument by the architects André and Jean Polak in 1957 at the Heysel-Plateau in Laeken near Brussels.\nStamp: Michel: No. 1091 ; Yvert &amp; Tellier: No. 1008A; Scott: No. 501; AFA: 1108\nColor: dark green\nWatermark: none\nNominal value: 2 F 50 (= 2.50 Francs)\nPostage validity: from 4 February 1958 until ?\n\nStamp picture size (printed area of a single stamp): 24.5 x 35.5 mm",
          "width": 920,
          "height": 1268,
          "mimeType": "image/jpeg",
          "license": "Public domain",
          "artist": "\"La Poste\" (Belgium) of the Belgian government",
          "sourceUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BEL_1958_MiNr1091_pm_B002.jpg",
          "sourceType": "core",
          "sourceArticleId": "expo-58-wp",
          "sourceGeohash4": "u151",
